TEMPLATE thompson_bible
# version: "1.0"
# author: "Thompson Chain Reference Bible"

# ============================================
# SOURCE FIELDS
# ============================================

SOURCE FIELDS
    OPTIONAL reference
END SOURCE FIELDS

FIELD reference TYPE TEXT
    SCOPE SOURCE
    DESCRIPTION Translation or edition of the Bible
    GUIDELINES
        Identify the translation or edition from which the verses are drawn.
        Use a short, stable label that names the work (e.g. Thompson Chain Reference Bible).
        Keep the same spelling across every reference to the same source.
        Do not include page numbers, volumes, or other location details here.
    END GUIDELINES
END FIELD

# ============================================
# ITEM FIELDS
# ============================================

ITEM FIELDS
    REQUIRED passage
    OPTIONAL text
    OPTIONAL topic
END ITEM FIELDS

FIELD passage TYPE TEXT
    SCOPE ITEM
    DESCRIPTION Biblical reference in USX format (e.g. Pro 12:23)
    GUIDELINES
        Record the verse reference in USX format: book abbreviation, chapter, and verse.
        Use the three-letter USX book code (e.g. Gen, Pro, Mat, Rev).
        Mark verse ranges with a hyphen (e.g. Gen 1:1-25) and single verses without one.
        Keep one space between the book code and the chapter number.
        Do not include the translation name or the verse text in this field.
    END GUIDELINES
END FIELD

FIELD text TYPE QUOTATION
    SCOPE ITEM
    DESCRIPTION Verse text from the translation
    GUIDELINES
        Quote the verse text literally and completely as it appears in the chosen translation.
        Preserve the original wording, punctuation, and spelling of the source.
        Include only the text of the verse named in the passage field, with no added commentary.
        Keep the quotation consistent with the edition declared in the source reference.
        Leave the field empty when the corpus indexes references only, without verse text.
    END GUIDELINES
END FIELD

FIELD topic TYPE CODE
    SCOPE ITEM
    DESCRIPTION Thompson chain topic(s) associated with the verse
    GUIDELINES
        Assign every chain topic that the verse genuinely belongs to.
        Use uppercase spelling with underscores for spaces (e.g. HEAVENS_THE_NATURAL).
        List multiple topics on one line, separated by a comma and a space (e.g. CREATOR, EARTH).
        Prefer topics already present in the ontology and reuse their exact spelling.
        Create a new topic only when the theme is distinct and has no ontology equivalent.
        Every topic applied must have a corresponding ONTOLOGY block.
    END GUIDELINES
END FIELD

# ============================================
# ONTOLOGY FIELDS
# ============================================

ONTOLOGY FIELDS
    OPTIONAL description
END ONTOLOGY FIELDS

FIELD description TYPE TEXT
    SCOPE ONTOLOGY
    DESCRIPTION Entry description when available
    GUIDELINES
        Define the topic concisely, identifying the biblical person, place, object, or theme.
        Lead with the essential category (e.g. son of Amram, the first high priest).
        Keep the definition independent of any single verse or chain.
        When homonyms exist, distinguish them to avoid topics with identical descriptions.
        Leave the field empty only when no reliable definition is available for the topic.
    END GUIDELINES
END FIELD